Previously, repo lookups would occur by an API call that could return a list of repos, filtered by the name and access level. A second lookup would then occur once the repo ID was found (to get an object that could actually be used to update the repo).

Now, the main path is to do a direct lookup with project/name (e.g. llnl/GRAPE), which is much faster. This path does not handle access level, so the other path is maintained as a fallback.

For an application, the runtime for \"grape approve\" retrieving modified repositories dropped from ~10 to ~5 seconds.

This update will likely improve the performance of other commands such as \"grape review\" and \"grape publish\".

